\par\par \b \uc2 Apple Staff in Maryland Vote Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ginger Adams Otis \par \uc2 365 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers at a unionized \uc2 Apple\uc2  retail store near Baltimore voted Saturday to authorize a strike as contract talks with the tech giant continue.\par \par \uc2 The yes vote allows the bargaining committee for the union that represents the store workers to call for a strike at any time. No date has yet been set for a potential work stoppage, according to a union representative. If the workers decide to strike, it would be the first walkout by \uc2 Apple\uc2  employees in the U.S. The Maryland store was the first in the U.S. to unionize in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The next round of contract talks between \uc2 Apple\uc2  and the local affiliate of the \uc2 International Association of Machinists & Aerospace Workers\uc2  is scheduled for May 21. The union, which represents approximately 100 employees at the Towson, Md., retail store, said its negotiations with \uc2 Apple\uc2  management began in January 2023.\par \par \uc2 "This vote today is the first step in demonstrating our solidarity and sends a clear message to \uc2 Apple\uc2 ," negotiating committee members said in a statement late Saturday. "We remain committed to securing tangible improvements that benefit all employees."\par \par \uc2 Workers at the Towson store voted in June 2022 to form a labor group, the Coalition of Organized Retail Employees. As the first U.S. Apple store to unionize, the group chose to join IAM.\par \par \uc2 Since then, the two sides have come to tentative agreements on 25 issues, among them topics such as how to handle grievance and arbitration cases, performance reviews, nondiscrimination policies and more, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 Talks have slowed down over core economic issues such as hourly wages, overtime, scheduling and shift premiums.\par \par \uc2 Apple\uc2  said on Saturday it would continue its good-faith engagement with the union representing Towson workers.\par \par \uc2 "We deeply value our team members and we're proud to provide them with industry leading compensation and exceptional benefits," the company statement said.\par \par \uc2 A second group of \uc2 Apple\uc2  retail workers in Oklahoma voted to unionize in October 2022, not long after Towson. The Oklahoma City store was the second out of more than 270 Apple U.S. stores to organize officially. Those workers joined the \uc2 Communications Workers of America\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240513ek5d0001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
