\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2 , \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  In Pact, Avert Potential Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Maloney and Ben Glickman \par \uc2 315 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 February 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Anheuser-Busch InBev\uc2  and the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  reached a tentative agreement on a new labor contract Wednesday, avoiding a potential strike of thousands of employees at breweries across the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , which represents about 5,000 brewery workers, had previously threatened to strike Friday if a deal wasn't reached by Thursday, when the current union contract expires. Members had been seeking pay increases and a guarantee that \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  wouldn't close breweries.\par \par \uc2 The tentative five-year labor pact, which is still subject to ratification by members, provides for a raise of $8 an hour, including an immediate $4-an-hour raise in the first year.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and the brewer said the deal provided "significant" job security for union members. They didn't say whether any breweries would close.\par \par \uc2 The union said the deal also would include a $2,500 ratification bonus, changes to health and retirement benefits and increased pension contributions.\par \par \uc2 Voting by union members is expected next week, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Anheuser-Busch\uc2  said the deal recognizes and rewards its employees while also positioning the company for long-term success. Hours after announcing the labor deal, the global beer giant reported that its U.S. revenue fell 17% in the latest quarter, primarily because of sluggish sales of Bud Light.\par \par \uc2 Bud Light's U.S. sales have been in a slump since a boycott began in April, when a transgender influencer posted an image on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  of a personalized can the brand had sent her as a gift.\par \par \uc2 AB InBev\uc2  fared better outside the U.S. Revenue grew 7% in the Asia Pacific region, 30% in South America and 12% in Europe, the Middle East and Africa.\par \par \uc2 Overall, the company's global revenue was $14.47 billion in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240229ek2t0001z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
