\par\par \b \uc2 FTC\uc2  Sues To Block Merger Of \uc2 Kroger\uc2 , \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  --- Supermarket chains' $25 billion tie-up would lead to higher prices, agency says\b0\par\par\uc2 By Patrick Thomas and Dave Michaels \par \uc2 1,146 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 February 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  sued to block \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's $25 billion bid for rival \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 , throwing into uncertainty the fate of the largest supermarket deal in history.\par \par \uc2 In a lawsuit filed in federal court in Oregon on Monday, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  said the deal would lead to higher food prices and harm union workers' bargaining power, and asked a court to block the companies from closing their deal on antitrust grounds. The companies' plan to address the government's concerns by selling hundreds of stores in Washington, Colorado and other states won't solve the problem, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Kroger\uc2 's acquisition of \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  would lead to additional grocery price hikes for everyday goods, further exacerbating the financial strain consumers across the country face today," said Henry Liu, director of the \uc2 FTC\uc2 's bureau of competition.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Kroger\uc2  spokeswoman said the \uc2 FTC\uc2 's decision makes it more likely that U.S. consumers will see higher food prices and fewer grocery stores, while strengthening nonunionized retailers. An \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  spokesman said the combined company would be a stronger competitor against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , \uc2 Walmart\uc2  and \uc2 Costco\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2 's challenge comes as the portion of U.S. consumers' income spent on food has reached a three-decade high, despite inflation easing for many other goods. President Biden, a Democrat who is running for re-election, took aim at large grocery chains in January over high food prices, saying stores are gouging shoppers and bringing in excess profits.\par \par \uc2 It signals a high-water mark for the role of labor in antitrust analysis, said \uc2 William Kovacic\uc2 , a former \uc2 FTC\uc2  chairman now at \uc2 George Washington University\uc2 . The FTC and Justice Department, which share antitrust enforcement duties, now probe whether mergers will lead to bigger employers with excessive leverage over workers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2 's claim that Kroger-Albertsons would have more power to neutralize the threat of a union boycott or strike is uncommon, Kovacic said. "Showcasing it directly [in an antitrust case] is new," he said.\par \par \uc2 The White House, which didn't comment on the lawsuit, said Biden is committed to lowering grocery costs using every tool at his disposal.\par \par \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  are the largest and second-largest U.S. supermarket operators in terms of sales. Based in Cincinnati, \uc2 Kroger\uc2  operates more than 2,700 grocery stores, including its namesake locations and regional chains such as Fred Meyer and Ralph's. \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  runs nearly 2,300 supermarkets across the U.S., including the chain \uc2 Safeway\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The two companies operate in many of the same areas, including Colorado, Southern California, Washington, Texas and Chicago. The deal, which includes the assumption of about $4.7 billion of \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 ' net debt, would be the grocery sector's largest ever, \uc2 Dealogic\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The suit sets up another battle for U.S. antitrust enforcers. Under the Biden administration, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  and the Justice Department have challenged megadeals ranging from \uc2 Microsoft\uc2 's bid for \uc2 Activision Blizzard\uc2  to \uc2 JetBlue\uc2 's attempted takeover of \uc2 Spirit Airlines\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2  and the Justice Department have a mixed record fighting mergers. DOJ won a string of recent cases, including getting a judge to block \uc2 JetBlue\uc2 's purchase of \uc2 Spirit\uc2 , and before that, \uc2 JetBlue\uc2 's proposed alliance with \uc2 American Airlines\uc2 . The \uc2 FTC\uc2  lost merger litigation contests with \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Meta Platforms\uc2  but prevailed in a lawsuit that blocked gene-sequencing company \uc2 Illumina\uc2  from buying cancer-blood-test maker \uc2 Grail\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The deal would be the second time \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  combined with a big rival, after it joined forces with \uc2 Safeway\uc2  in 2015. The \uc2 FTC\uc2  allowed that deal to close but required \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  to sell 168 stores to a little-known grocery chain that later went bankrupt. The outcome embarrassed the \uc2 FTC\uc2  and led consumer advocates and unions to repeatedly highlight the risk posed by a suggested fix by \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 To try to alleviate antitrust concerns, \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  announced in September a nearly $2 billion deal to sell 413 stores to \uc2 C&S Wholesale Grocers\uc2 , one of the largest U.S. grocery-supply companies, which owns some stores under the Grand Union and Piggly Wiggly brands. In January, the companies told regional union leaders the divestiture plan was upped to 510 stores.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2  said \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  proposed to sell off "a hodgepodge of unconnected stores, banners, brands and other assets that \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's antitrust lawyers have cobbled together." C&S currently operates 23 supermarkets and one retail pharmacy, the \uc2 FTC\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 A court will have to decide how much competition is lost to the merger -- and that will turn on how it defines the options for consumers. The \uc2 FTC\uc2  is likely to argue \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  compete in a narrower segment of traditional supermarkets, while the companies will say they fight for customers with discounters and warehouse clubs such as \uc2 Costco\uc2  and \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , said David Olson, a professor at Boston College Law School. "There is good evidence that the defendants here can cite to say the market should be broader, and there is also evidence that online shopping for groceries has expanded," he said.\par \par \uc2 Analysts at investment research firm \uc2 Capstone\uc2  said the companies face slim odds of prevailing in court and would likely need to divest more than 650 stores to secure approval.\par \par \uc2 If the deal is terminated, \uc2 Kroger\uc2  will have to pay \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  $600 million. Shares of \uc2 Kroger\uc2  finished nearly 2% lower on Monday, while \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  gained about 0.6%.\par \par \uc2 A judge in Oregon will decide whether to grant the \uc2 FTC\uc2 's request for a preliminary injunction that would suspend the deal from closing. That process normally takes several months. Attorneys general in Washington and Colorado sued to stop the merger. Nine states including California joined the \uc2 FTC\uc2 's case on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The tie-up aims to bolster the grocers' scale, technology, and leverage in negotiations with suppliers, according to industry executives. The companies have said that \uc2 Walmart\uc2 's grocery market share is twice the size of a combined \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Regional leaders for The United Food and Commercial Workers International Union, the biggest U.S. union representing grocery workers, opposed \uc2 Kroger\uc2 's deal for \uc2 Albertsons\uc2 , saying it would hurt workers, shoppers and the food-supply chain. Some union leaders expressed concerns about the viability of stores the companies divest.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FTC\uc2  said \uc2 Kroger\uc2  and \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  would have more leverage to impose subpar terms on union workers that slow wage increases, worsen benefits and potentially degrade working conditions. The companies have said the only parties that would benefit if the deal is blocked would be large, nonunion retailers.\par \par \uc2 This month, a regional \uc2 UFCW\uc2  chapter for several West Coast states said it supported the deal. The union said it figures \uc2 Albertsons\uc2  eventually would be acquired by another company, and the deal with \uc2 Kroger\uc2  would be the best outcome.\par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw380\pich325\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal5700\pichgoal4875
