\par\par \b \uc2 Latest \uc2 Wayfair\uc2  Layoffs Hit Its Remote Workers Hardest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sarah Nassauer and Paul Berger \par \uc2 368 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Wayfair\uc2  employees who work remotely were more likely to be laid off in the latest round of job cuts at the online furniture seller, executives told staff on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Wayfair\uc2  executives hosted an all-hands meeting to discuss recent layoffs that cut 13% of its workforce and face employee questions about the layoffs and the company's financial future, people familiar with the situation said.\par \par \uc2 Workers asked about the tone and timing of a memo Chief Executive \uc2 Niraj Shah\uc2  sent to staff in December, weeks before the layoffs were announced, in which he asked them to work harder. Shah said on Tuesday that people needed to continue to put in hard work if they expected a positive outcome for the company and for themselves.\par \par \uc2 Other workers asked about the company's longer-term financial health. A sale isn't being considered, said co-founder \uc2 Steve Conine\uc2 , a co-chairman of the board. "If bankruptcy is inevitable then shame on all of us for not working harder," he quipped from a stage in the company's Boston headquarters. Conine was trying to emphasize that the future of the company is in \uc2 Wayfair\uc2 's control, said a company spokeswoman.\par \par \uc2 Last week, \uc2 Wayfair\uc2  said it would lay off around 1,650 workers, its fourth significant layoff since 2020. Soaring demand early in the pandemic fueled growth, but sales and profits have since stagnated.\par \par \uc2 "We went overboard in hiring during a strong economic period and veered away from our core principles, and while we have come quite far back to them, we are not quite there," Shah said in a memo to staff last week.\par \par \uc2 Wayfair\uc2 's stock rose after it announced the latest layoffs but is down more than 80% from its record of about $345 a share, hit in early 2021. For nearly two years each quarter's profit has been lower than that of a year earlier.\par \par \uc2 At the meeting on Tuesday, Shah said the company continues to have some remote roles but has figured out which ones make sense in-person. Executives said they believe most workers should be at the office on most days.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020240124ek1o00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
